@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# mypy RATCHET — files that MUST stay type-clean under the CI flag set.
+#
+# WHY THIS EXISTS
+#   `core/pyproject.toml` has declared `[tool.mypy] strict = true` for a long
+#   time, but no workflow ever invoked mypy. The config was decorative: 400k+
+#   lines of Python shipping with 434 `# type: ignore` comments and no
+#   type-level regression detection at all.
+#
+#   A big-bang `mypy core/` would fail with thousands of pre-existing errors
+#   and be switched off within a week. So this is a ratchet: only files listed
+#   here are enforced, every listed file is CLEAN today, and the list may only
+#   GROW. Removing a file is not allowed without deleting the module.
+#
+# HOW TO ADD A FILE
+#   1. mypy --ignore-missing-imports --follow-imports=skip --no-error-summary <file>
+#   2. Fix (not silence) the errors — a bare `# type: ignore` without an error
+#      code is rejected by scripts/ci/check_mypy_ratchet.py.
+#   3. Append the path below, alphabetically.
+#
+# Verified clean against core @ b25da39 with mypy 2.4.1:
+core/config_control_plane.py
+core/config_parsers.py
+core/config_registry.py
+core/config_validator.py
+core/health_policy.py
+core/intent.py
+core/intent_router.py
+core/intent_router_v2.py
